message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Terrain-based clustering of archaeological surface finds"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
authors:
  - family-names: "Cerrillo Cuenca"
    given-names: "Enrique"
    email: "enriqcer@ucm.es"
    affiliation: "Complutense University of Madrid"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2476-0472"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ecerrillo/landscape-clustering-pipeline"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Landscape analysis pipeline for archaeological surface survey data. From a
  LiDAR-derived DEM it computes slope and topographic position, classifies the
  terrain into erosion–transport–deposition zones, and clusters surface finds
  with HDBSCAN over a terrain-cost distance matrix. It includes a sensitivity
  analysis of the clustering and a cell-scale negative binomial model of the
  association between prehistoric and historic finds, together with a sample
  dataset (PNOA-derived DEM tile and 225 points) for end-to-end verification.
keywords:
  - archaeology
  - surface survey
  - HDBSCAN
  - spatial analysis
